IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcdd-dates`

-- Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act 1942 (NSW) -- the claims machinery, from the seat of the person who claims:
-- the worker disabled by a dust disease, or the dependant of a worker who died.
--
-- SEAT: the claimant. Every exported question is one that person would ask: "Is my disease a dust disease?", "Am I
-- entitled to an award?", "Are we entitled after my partner's death?", "By when must the Authority decide?", "How much
-- is the lump sum?", "Is the weekly payment for my child still payable?", "Do I have to tell the Authority about other
-- compensation, and by when?", "By when must I appeal?". The Authority, the Medical Assessment Panel and the District
-- Court get no seat: their certificates, findings and discretions are inputs, answered conditionally.
--
-- Provisions: s 3 (dust disease, worker, spouse); Sch 1 (the diseases); s 8(1) (entitlement of the worker and of the
-- dependants), (1A), (1AA) (the time to decide), (2)(c)(ii) (partial disablement before death), (2A) (funeral),
-- (2B) (lump sum and weekly payments for a spouse or other prescribed relative and children), (2D)(b) (who is paid for a
-- child), (2E) (redemption), (3A) (date of injury), (3B) (partial treated as total), (6) (no double compensation),
-- (6A) (reduced rate), (7), (8) (from when weekly payments run), (9) (prescribed relative); s 8AA (compensation
-- elsewhere); s 8B (interim award); s 8I (appeal); s 9A (examination costs); s 11 (diseases added to Sch 1); Sch 2
-- cll 20, 21 (retired workers). The rates themselves are in the Workers Compensation Act 1987 (the Principal Act), a
-- separate subject: they are asked as inputs. Out, with reasons in NOTES.md: the Authority, the Board, the Fund and its
-- contributions (ss 5-7, 6), s 8E and Sch 1A (the third party's duties to the Authority), regulation-making (s 10),
-- repeals and spent transitional provisions.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "where", "if", "only if", "unless" or "until", a flat "shall not"), or NOTHING where the Act
-- does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 18 October 2022; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act 1942`

§§ `The nouns`

-- Schedule 1 "Dust diseases", in the Schedule's order, and the s 3 extension ("includes any pathological condition of
-- the lungs, pleura or peritoneum, that is caused by dust that may also cause a disease so specified").
DECLARE `The disease` IS ONE OF
    `aluminosis`
    `asbestosis`
    `asbestos induced carcinoma`
    `asbestos related pleural diseases`
    `bagassosis`
    `berylliosis`
    `byssinosis`
    `coal dust pneumoconiosis`
    `diffuse dust-related pulmonary fibrosis`
    `farmers lung`
    `hard metal pneumoconiosis`
    `hypersensitivity pneumonitis`
    `mesothelioma`
    `pneumoconiosis of any form`
    `silica-induced carcinoma of the lung`
    `silicosis`
    `silico-tuberculosis`
    `systemic sclerosis`
    `talcosis`
    `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum caused by dust that can also cause a listed disease`
    `some other disease or condition`

-- The Medical Assessment Panel's certificate of disablement (s 8(1)(a)).
DECLARE `The panel's certificate of disablement` IS ONE OF
    `the panel certifies me totally disabled for work from a dust disease`
    `the panel certifies me partially disabled for work from a dust disease`
    `the panel has not certified me disabled for work from a dust disease`

-- Whether the person was a "worker" during the time engaged in the occupation (s 8(1)(a)(i), (ii)).
DECLARE `Time as a worker in the occupation` IS ONE OF
    `a worker for the whole of the time`
    `a worker for only part of the time`
    `never a worker in that occupation`

-- s 8(1)(c)(ii)(a): what the panel did, where the person who died had applied before death.
DECLARE `The panel's certificate before death` IS ONE OF
    `the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease`
    `the panel had not examined them but certifies after death that they were disabled from a dust disease`
    `the panel has not certified them disabled from a dust disease`

-- The answer to "are we entitled after the death?" (s 8(1)(b), (c)).
DECLARE `Entitlement after the death` IS ONE OF
    `entitled under section 8(1)(b), death from a dust disease`
    `entitled under section 8(1)(c), death of a person disabled by a dust disease`
    `entitled under section 8(1)(c), but the Authority may refuse all or part because they refused an examination`
    `not entitled under section 8(1)`

-- The answer to "has the Authority decided in time?" (s 8(1A), (1AA)).
DECLARE `The Authority's decision time` IS ONE OF
    `decided within the 2 working days`
    `decided late, but the decision is not invalid for that reason`
    `not yet decided, and the 2 working days have not ended`
    `not yet decided, and the 2 working days have ended`

-- s 3 "Spouse": legally married, or (for claims after the 1998 amendment) a de facto partner.
DECLARE `My relationship to the worker` IS ONE OF
    `legally married to the worker`
    `the worker's de facto partner`
    `neither`

-- s 8(2B)(a): who depended on the worker immediately before death.
DECLARE `Who depended on the worker` IS ONE OF
    `a surviving spouse and no one else`
    `a surviving spouse and one or more children and no one else`
    `one relative named in section 8(9)(b)(ii) and no one else`
    `two or more relatives named in section 8(9)(b)(ii) and no one else`
    `one or more children and no one else`
    `some other person or combination of persons`

-- s 8(2B)(b), (c): the award the lump sum is under.
DECLARE `The death award` IS ONE OF
    `an award under section 8(1)(b)`
    `an award under section 8(1)(c), the disablement having been total`
    `an award under section 8(1)(c), the disablement having been partial`

-- s 8(2B)(b)(i) and Sch 2 cll 13, 14: when the worker died, for the rate in force at the death (s 8(2B)(d1)).
DECLARE `When the worker died` IS ONE OF
    `in the first 12 months after the 2010 amending Act commenced`
    `in the second 12 months after the 2010 amending Act commenced`
    `after those 24 months but before 1 April 2013`
    `on or after 1 April 2013`

-- s 8(2D)(b): who is paid the weekly payment for a child.
DECLARE `Who is paid for the child` IS ONE OF
    `the surviving spouse`
    `the person or institution the Authority directs`

-- s 8AA(1): a "prescribed engagement".
DECLARE `How I was engaged when I contracted the disease` IS ONE OF
    `as a Commonwealth employee under Commonwealth employees compensation law`
    `under a contract of service or apprenticeship outside New South Wales`
    `in some other way`

-- The answer to "have I told the Authority in time?" (s 8AA(3)).
DECLARE `What section 8AA(3) means for me` IS ONE OF
    `section 8AA(3) puts no duty on me`
    `I informed the Authority within the 7 days`
    `I have not informed the Authority within the 7 days, an offence with a maximum penalty of 1 penalty unit`
    `I have not yet informed the Authority, and the 7 days have not ended`

-- s 9A: the costs of submitting for an examination.
DECLARE `The examination cost` IS ONE OF
    `wages I lost by submitting for the examination`
    `fares, travelling expenses or maintenance`
    `some other cost`

-- Sch 2 cl 20(1): why the worker is retired.
DECLARE `Why I am retired` IS ONE OF
    `I reached an applicable retirement age`
    `I am unfit for suitable employment as a result of a dust disease`
    `some other reason`

-- Sch 2 cl 21: the wage figure used for weekly payments during total incapacity.
DECLARE `The wage figure` IS ONE OF
    `the ABS average weekly total cash earnings of all NSW employees for the week before I was incapacitated`
    `my actual wages, worked out under section 42 of the 1987 Act at my request`
    `clause 21 does not apply to me`

-- The parties and acts of the three regulative rules.
DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF `the Authority`, `the claimant`
DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF
    `decide whether to accept or refuse the claim`
    `inform the Authority of the other compensation`
    `appeal to the District Court`

§§ `s 3, Sch 1 -- the definitions`

-- s 3(1) "Dust disease means any disease specified in Schedule 1, and includes any pathological condition of the lungs,
-- pleura or peritoneum, that is caused by dust that may also cause a disease so specified." A "means" definition with an
-- "includes" widening: anything outside both is JUST FALSE (fork F1). Schedule 1 may be amended by regulation (s 10(3));
-- the list is the deposited one.
@export Is my disease a dust disease under the Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act (s 3, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `my disease` IS A `The disease` @desc The disease or condition you have. One of: "aluminosis", "asbestosis", "asbestos induced carcinoma", "asbestos related pleural diseases", "bagassosis", "berylliosis", "byssinosis", "coal dust pneumoconiosis", "diffuse dust-related pulmonary fibrosis", "farmers lung", "hard metal pneumoconiosis", "hypersensitivity pneumonitis", "mesothelioma", "pneumoconiosis of any form", "silica-induced carcinoma of the lung", "silicosis", "silico-tuberculosis", "systemic sclerosis", "talcosis", "another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum caused by dust that can also cause a listed disease", "some other disease or condition"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my disease a dust disease` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my disease`
    WHEN `some other disease or condition` THEN JUST FALSE  -- a "means" definition (fork F1)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 3(1) "worker does not include a worker in or about a mine." Otherwise "worker" is the Principal Act's term (s 1(1):
-- the Act "shall be construed with" the Workers Compensation Act 1987), a borrowed term asked as a fact.
@export Am I a "worker" for the Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act (s 3)?
GIVEN `I was a worker under the workers compensation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a "worker" as the Workers Compensation Act 1987 and the 1998 Act use the word (in general, an employee under a contract of service or apprenticeship, not a self-employed person)
      `I worked in or about a mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you worked in or about a mine (a coal mine within the old Coal Mines Regulation Act 1982 meaning)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a worker under the Act` MEANS
    IF `I worked in or about a mine`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- a flat "does not include"
    ELSE IF `I was a worker under the workers compensation legislation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- the borrowed term, answered by the fact given

-- s 3(1) "Spouse of a person means (a) where the claim ... was made ... before the commencement of Schedule 6 [2] to the
-- [1998 amending Act]--a person to whom the person is legally married, or (b) where the claim ... was made ... after
-- that commencement--(i) a person to whom the person is legally married, or (ii) the de facto partner of the person."
-- "De facto partner" (Interpretation Act 1987 s 21C) is a borrowed term, asked.
@export Am I the worker's "spouse" for a claim under the Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act (s 3)?
GIVEN `my relationship to the worker` IS A `My relationship to the worker` @desc Your relationship to the worker. One of: "legally married to the worker", "the worker's de facto partner", "neither"
      `the claim was made after the 1998 amendment commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim was made after Schedule 6 [2] to the Workers Compensation Legislation Amendment (Dust Diseases and Other Matters) Act 1998 commenced (true for any claim made in this century)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I the worker's spouse under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my relationship to the worker`
    WHEN `legally married to the worker` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the worker's de facto partner` THEN
        IF `the claim was made after the 1998 amendment commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE  -- a "means" definition
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- a "means" definition

§§ `s 8(1)(a) -- the worker's own award`

-- s 8(1) "Subject to this Act--(a) where the Medical Assessment Panel certifies that a person is totally or partially
-- disabled for work from a dust disease and that the person's disablement was reasonably attributable to the person's
-- exposure to the inhalation of dust in an occupation to the nature of which the disease was due, such person shall, if
-- the Authority finds--(i) that such person was a worker during the whole of the time the person was engaged in such
-- occupation, or (ii) that such person was a worker during only part of the time ..., and, on the report of the Medical
-- Assessment Panel, further finds that the person's disablement was reasonably attributable to the person's exposure ...
-- during the time that the Authority has found that the person was a worker in such occupation, be entitled to an award
-- from the Authority, and to receive compensation at the prescribed rates from the Fund". "Where" and "if": a failed
-- condition is JUST FALSE. The panel's certificate is conclusive, subject to appeal (s 7(5)).
GIVEN `the panel's certificate` IS A `The panel's certificate of disablement`
      `the panel certifies attribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my time as a worker` IS A `Time as a worker in the occupation`
      `the Authority finds attribution to my time as a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker has an entitlement under section 8(1)(a)` IF
        `the panel certifies disablement`
    AND `the panel certifies attribution`
    AND `the Authority's finding about worker time is made`
    WHERE
        `the panel certifies disablement` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the panel's certificate`
            WHEN `the panel has not certified me disabled for work from a dust disease` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the Authority's finding about worker time is made` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my time as a worker`
            WHEN `a worker for the whole of the time` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a worker for only part of the time` THEN `the Authority finds attribution to my time as a worker`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Am I entitled to an award of compensation from the Dust Diseases Authority for my disablement (s 8(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the panel's certificate` IS A `The panel's certificate of disablement` @desc What the Medical Assessment Panel has certified about you. One of: "the panel certifies me totally disabled for work from a dust disease", "the panel certifies me partially disabled for work from a dust disease", "the panel has not certified me disabled for work from a dust disease"
      `the panel certifies attribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the panel certifies that your disablement was reasonably attributable to your exposure to the inhalation of dust in an occupation to the nature of which the disease was due
      `my time as a worker` IS A `Time as a worker in the occupation` @desc Whether the Authority finds you were a worker (an employee, not in or about a mine) while you were engaged in that occupation. One of: "a worker for the whole of the time", "a worker for only part of the time", "never a worker in that occupation"
      `the Authority finds attribution to my time as a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were a worker for only part of the time: whether the Authority, on the panel's report, finds your disablement reasonably attributable to your exposure to dust during the time you were a worker
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to an award for my disablement` MEANS
    IF `the worker has an entitlement under section 8(1)(a)` `the panel's certificate` `the panel certifies attribution` `my time as a worker` `the Authority finds attribution to my time as a worker`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- "where ... certifies" and "if the Authority finds"

§§ `s 8(1)(b), (c) -- the dependants' award after a death`

-- s 8(1)(b): where the panel certifies that a person died from a dust disease, the death reasonably attributable to the
-- exposure, the dependants are entitled if the Authority finds the person a worker the whole time, or part of the time
-- with the death attributable to that part. s 8(1)(c): where a person dies and (i) was receiving, or entitled under an
-- award to, continuing payments for disablement from a dust disease, or (ii)(a) had applied before death and the panel
-- certified disablement (after examining them before death, or after death without having examined them) and (b) the
-- Authority finds the person a worker the whole time, or part of the time and the panel further certifies
-- attribution to that part, the dependants are entitled "if they are not entitled under paragraph (b)". The proviso:
-- the Authority "may refuse ... the whole or any part" for a person under (c)(ii)(a)(i) who, after the last examination,
-- refused, neglected or failed without reasonable cause to submit for examination when asked. "Dependants" is the
-- Principal Act's term, asked. The proviso is a discretion: answered conditionally.
@export After the death of a worker on whom I depended, am I entitled to an award as a dependant, and under which paragraph (s 8(1)(b), (c))?
GIVEN `I was a dependant of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a dependant of the person who died (wholly or partly dependent on their earnings, as the Workers Compensation Act 1987 uses the word)
      `the panel certifies death from a dust disease attributable to the occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Medical Assessment Panel certifies that the person died from a dust disease and that the death was reasonably attributable to their exposure to the inhalation of dust in an occupation to the nature of which the disease was due
      `they were receiving continuing payments for a dust disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before death, the person was receiving, or was entitled under an award to receive, continuing payments of compensation from the Fund for disablement for work from a dust disease
      `they had applied before death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before death, the person had applied to the Authority (or the former Silicosis Committee) for compensation or to be examined by the Medical Assessment Panel
      `the panel's certificate before death` IS A `The panel's certificate before death` @desc What the panel certified about the person's disablement (with the disablement reasonably attributable to exposure to dust in the occupation). One of: "the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease", "the panel had not examined them but certifies after death that they were disabled from a dust disease", "the panel has not certified them disabled from a dust disease"
      `their time as a worker` IS A `Time as a worker in the occupation` @desc Whether the Authority finds the person was a worker while engaged in the occupation. One of: "a worker for the whole of the time", "a worker for only part of the time", "never a worker in that occupation"
      `the death or disablement is attributed to their time as a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If they were a worker for only part of the time: whether it is found (by the Authority on the panel's report, or certified by the panel) that the death or disablement was reasonably attributable to exposure to dust while they were a worker
      `they refused an examination without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the panel's last examination of them, the person refused, neglected or failed without reasonable cause to submit for examination when the Authority asked
GIVETH AN `Entitlement after the death`
`Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I was a dependant of the person who died`) THEN `not entitled under section 8(1)`
           IF `the panel certifies death from a dust disease attributable to the occupation` AND `the worker time finding` THEN `entitled under section 8(1)(b), death from a dust disease`
           IF `they were receiving continuing payments for a dust disease` THEN `entitled under section 8(1)(c), death of a person disabled by a dust disease`
           IF `they had applied before death` AND `the worker time finding` THEN
               CONSIDER `the panel's certificate before death`
               WHEN `the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease` THEN
                   IF `they refused an examination without reasonable cause`
                   THEN `entitled under section 8(1)(c), but the Authority may refuse all or part because they refused an examination`
                   ELSE `entitled under section 8(1)(c), death of a person disabled by a dust disease`
               WHEN `the panel had not examined them but certifies after death that they were disabled from a dust disease` THEN `entitled under section 8(1)(c), death of a person disabled by a dust disease`
               OTHERWISE `not entitled under section 8(1)`
           OTHERWISE `not entitled under section 8(1)`  -- "where" and "if": the text's no
    WHERE
        `the worker time finding` MEANS
            CONSIDER `their time as a worker`
            WHEN `a worker for the whole of the time` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a worker for only part of the time` THEN `the death or disablement is attributed to their time as a worker`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 8(1A), (1AA) -- the time for the Authority's decision`

-- s 8(1A) "The Authority is to decide whether to accept or refuse a claim for compensation within 2 working days after--
-- (a) the Medical Assessment Panel issues a certificate under subsection (1), or (b) the Authority is provided with the
-- information required by the Authority to enable the claim to be determined, whichever is the later." (1AA) "However
-- any decision by the Authority made after that 2-day period in respect of the claim is not invalid merely because of
-- when it is made." Working days: fork F7.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 8(1A) -- the Authority is to decide the claim within 2 working days` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Authority`
    MUST `decide whether to accept or refuse the claim`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Authority` BECAUSE "the claim was not decided within 2 working days after the later of the panel's certificate and the information the Authority required (s 8(1A)); the decision is not invalid for that reason (s 8(1AA))"

@export By what day must the Dust Diseases Authority decide whether to accept or refuse my claim (s 8(1A))?
GIVEN `the day the panel issued its certificate` IS A DATE @desc The day the Medical Assessment Panel issued its certificate about you under s 8(1)
      `the day the Authority had the information it required` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority was given the information it required to determine your claim
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the Authority decide my claim` MEANS
    `the working day` 2 `after` (`the later of` `the day the panel issued its certificate` `and` `the day the Authority had the information it required`)

@export Has the Dust Diseases Authority decided my claim within the 2 working days, and is a late decision still valid (s 8(1A), (1AA))?
GIVEN `the day the panel issued its certificate` IS A DATE @desc The day the Medical Assessment Panel issued its certificate about you under s 8(1)
      `the day the Authority had the information it required` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority was given the information it required to determine your claim
      `the Authority has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has decided to accept or refuse your claim
      `the day the Authority decided` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority decided (any day if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `The Authority's decision time`
`Was my claim decided in time` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has decided`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 8(1A) -- the Authority is to decide the claim within 2 working days` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Authority` `decide whether to accept or refuse the claim` `the decision time`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `decided within the 2 working days`
         OTHERWISE `decided late, but the decision is not invalid for that reason`
    ELSE IF `the days from` `the start` `to` `today` AT MOST `the days allowed`
         THEN `not yet decided, and the 2 working days have not ended`
         ELSE `not yet decided, and the 2 working days have ended`
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS `the later of` `the day the panel issued its certificate` `and` `the day the Authority had the information it required`
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the start` `to` (`By when must the Authority decide my claim` `the day the panel issued its certificate` `the day the Authority had the information it required`)
        `the raw decision time` MEANS `the days from` `the start` `to` `the day the Authority decided`
        `the decision time` MEANS IF `the raw decision time` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `the raw decision time`

§§ `s 8(2), (2A) -- the rates that follow the 1987 Act, and the funeral`

-- s 8(2): the rates are those of the Principal Act (weekly payments: Div 2 of Part 3 and Sch 6; death benefits: Div 1 of
-- Part 3 and Sch 6, as at the date of death; medical, hospital, rehabilitation and ambulance: Div 3 of Part 3). Those
-- figures are not in this Act and are asked. s 8(2)(c)(ii): where a person dies under s 8(1)(c) with a partial
-- disablement, "such percentage of the compensation payments that would have been payable under subparagraph (i) had
-- the disablement been total as is equal to the percentage of the person's disablement ... as certified by the Medical
-- Assessment Panel". A percentage outside 0 to 100 is not a percentage of disablement: NOTHING.
@export My relative died while partially disabled by a dust disease: how much of the full death benefit is payable (s 8(2)(c)(ii))?
GIVEN `the death benefit had the disablement been total` IS A NUMBER @desc The death benefit, in dollars, that would have been payable under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 (Div 1 of Part 3 and Sch 6, as in force at the date of death) had the disablement been total
      `the certified percentage of disablement` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of disablement for work from the dust disease that the Medical Assessment Panel certified (at its last examination before death, or in its certificate after death), from 0 to 100
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of the death benefit is payable for a partial disablement` MEANS
    IF `the certified percentage of disablement` LESS THAN 0 OR `the certified percentage of disablement` GREATER THAN 100
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (not a percentage of disablement; the text is silent)
    ELSE JUST ((`the death benefit had the disablement been total` TIMES `the certified percentage of disablement`) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 8(2A) "The Authority is to pay from the Fund the reasonable expenses of a deceased person's funeral not exceeding the
-- sum prescribed by or under section 26 of the Principal Act, but only if--(a) the person had dependants and those
-- dependants are entitled to an award under subsection (1), or (b) the person had no dependants, but any dependants of
-- the person (had they existed) would have been entitled to an award under subsection (1)." "Only if": failing both,
-- nothing is paid (0). Reasonableness is the Authority's judgment, asked as the amount found reasonable.
@export How much of the funeral expenses of the person who died will the Dust Diseases Authority pay (s 8(2A))?
GIVEN `the person had dependants entitled to an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died had dependants who are entitled to an award under s 8(1)
      `the person had no dependants, but dependants would have been entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person had no dependants, but dependants (had there been any) would have been entitled to an award under s 8(1)
      `the reasonable funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The funeral expenses, in dollars, found to be reasonable
      `the section 26 maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum funeral sum, in dollars, prescribed by or under section 26 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 (not in this Act)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of the funeral expenses will be paid` MEANS
    IF `the person had dependants entitled to an award` OR `the person had no dependants, but dependants would have been entitled`
    THEN `the smaller of` `the reasonable funeral expenses` `and` `the section 26 maximum`
    ELSE 0  -- "but only if"

§§ `s 8(2B), (2D), (2E), (9) -- the lump sum and weekly payments for a spouse or other relative`

-- s 8(9) "prescribed relative of a person means--(a) where the person died before the commencement of Schedule 6 [12] to
-- the [1998 amending Act]--a surviving spouse of the person, or (b) where the person dies after that commencement--(i) a
-- surviving spouse of the person, or (ii) if there is no surviving spouse of the person--a father, mother, grandfather,
-- grandmother, step-father, step-mother, grandson, granddaughter, brother, sister, half-brother or half-sister".
-- s 8(2B)(a): the subsection applies to an award under (1)(b) or (c) for a death "upon whom there was dependent for
-- support, immediately before the worker's death, the following and no other person or persons--(i) a prescribed relative
-- of the worker, or (ii) a surviving spouse and a child or children of the worker." A closed list: JUST FALSE outside it.
-- Two or more relatives under s 8(9)(b)(ii) with no spouse: "a prescribed relative" may mean one only -- NOTHING
-- (fork F3). Children alone: s 8(2AA) sends them to the ordinary s 8(2) rates, so JUST FALSE.
@export Does section 8(2B) (the lump sum and weekly payments for a surviving spouse or other close relative) apply to the award for the worker's death (s 8(2B)(a), (9))?
GIVEN `who depended on the worker` IS A `Who depended on the worker` @desc Who was dependent on the worker for support immediately before the death. One of: "a surviving spouse and no one else", "a surviving spouse and one or more children and no one else", "one relative named in section 8(9)(b)(ii) and no one else" (a father, mother, grandfather, grandmother, step-father, step-mother, grandson, granddaughter, brother, sister, half-brother or half-sister, where there is no surviving spouse), "two or more relatives named in section 8(9)(b)(ii) and no one else", "one or more children and no one else", "some other person or combination of persons"
      `the worker died after the 1998 amendment commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker died after Schedule 6 [12] to the Workers Compensation Legislation Amendment (Dust Diseases and Other Matters) Act 1998 commenced (true for any death in this century)
      `the award is under section 8(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the award for the death is made under s 8(1)(b) or (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does section 8(2B) apply` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the award is under section 8(1)(b) or (c)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `who depended on the worker`
         WHEN `a surviving spouse and no one else` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a surviving spouse and one or more children and no one else` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `one relative named in section 8(9)(b)(ii) and no one else` THEN
             IF `the worker died after the 1998 amendment commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 8(9)(a), a "means" definition
         WHEN `two or more relatives named in section 8(9)(b)(ii) and no one else` THEN
             IF `the worker died after the 1998 amendment commenced`
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind ("a prescribed relative": one, or each of several? fork F3)
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN `one or more children and no one else` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 8(2AA); a closed list
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- "the following and no other person or persons"

-- s 8(2B)(b)(i) "(A) during the period of 12 months starting on the commencement of the [2010 amending Act] (the first 12
-- months)--the amount of $268,375, or (B) during the period of 12 months (the second 12 months) that starts at the end
-- of the first 12 months--the amount of $291,040, or (C) after the end of the second 12 months--the amount of $311,050".
-- (d1): the rate in force at the time of the worker's death. Sch 2 cl 13(2): a death between the Bill's introduction
-- and assent is deemed to be on the day of assent. Sch 2 cl 14 and s 8(3)(d): the amount is indexed under Div 6 of
-- Part 3 of the Principal Act from 1 April 2013; the indexed figures are published by notice and are not deposited, so
-- they are asked.
GIVEN `when the worker died` IS A `When the worker died`
      `the indexed amount at the death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the section 8(2B)(b)(i) amount` `when the worker died` `the indexed amount at the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when the worker died`
    WHEN `in the first 12 months after the 2010 amending Act commenced` THEN JUST 268375
    WHEN `in the second 12 months after the 2010 amending Act commenced` THEN JUST 291040
    WHEN `after those 24 months but before 1 April 2013` THEN JUST 311050
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the indexed amount at the death` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST `the indexed amount at the death`
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the indexed figure is outside the deposited sources)

-- s 8(2B)(b): wholly dependent, award under (1)(b): the (b)(i) amount. (c): award under (1)(c): (i) total -- the (b)
-- amounts; (ii) partial -- the certified percentage of them. (d): partly dependent -- "such payments, not exceeding in
-- any case the amount that would have been payable ... had that person been wholly dependent ..., as may be determined
-- by the Authority to be reasonable and proportionate": the answer is then the most the Authority may award. Whether
-- the dependence was whole or partial therefore does not change the figure returned, and is not asked.
@export If section 8(2B) applies to the award for the worker's death, what is the lump sum for me as the surviving spouse or other close relative, or, if I was only partly dependent, the most it can be (s 8(2B)(b)(i), (c), (d), (d1))?
GIVEN `the award` IS A `The death award` @desc The award for the death. One of: "an award under section 8(1)(b)" (death from a dust disease), "an award under section 8(1)(c), the disablement having been total", "an award under section 8(1)(c), the disablement having been partial"
      `the certified percentage of disablement` IS A NUMBER @desc For a partial disablement under s 8(1)(c): the percentage of disablement the Medical Assessment Panel certified, from 0 to 100 (any number otherwise)
      `when the worker died` IS A `When the worker died` @desc When the worker died, measured from the commencement of the Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Amendment Act 2010 (a death between the Bill's introduction and assent counts as on the day of assent). One of: "in the first 12 months after the 2010 amending Act commenced", "in the second 12 months after the 2010 amending Act commenced", "after those 24 months but before 1 April 2013", "on or after 1 April 2013"
      `the indexed amount at the death` IS A NUMBER @desc For a death on or after 1 April 2013: the s 8(2B)(b)(i) amount as indexed under Division 6 of Part 3 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 and in force on the day of death, in dollars (0 if you do not know it)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most my section 8(2B) lump sum can be` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the award`
    WHEN `an award under section 8(1)(c), the disablement having been partial` THEN
        IF `the certified percentage of disablement` LESS THAN 0 OR `the certified percentage of disablement` GREATER THAN 100
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (not a percentage of disablement)
        ELSE CONSIDER `the full amount`
             WHEN JUST a THEN JUST ((a TIMES `the certified percentage of disablement`) DIVIDED BY 100)
             OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the indexed figure is outside the deposited sources)
    OTHERWISE `the full amount`
    WHERE
        `the full amount` MEANS `the section 8(2B)(b)(i) amount` `when the worker died` `the indexed amount at the death`

-- s 8(2B)(b)(ii) "in the case of a surviving spouse--a weekly payment of $137.30 per week, to continue until the marriage
-- or death, whichever event first occurs, of that person". (bb) "The payment ... is not to be made to a person during
-- any period when the person lives with another person on a permanent and bona fide domestic basis, although not legally
-- married to that other person." "Until" and a flat "is not to be made": JUST FALSE. The amount is an adjustable amount
-- (s 8(3)(d)); s 8(2G) took it to be $141.40 from 1 July 1992 (finding 2), so the figure in force is from the indexation
-- notices and is not computed. Partly dependent: (d), the Authority's determination: NOTHING.
@export If section 8(2B) applies and I am the worker's surviving spouse, is the weekly spouse payment payable to me now (s 8(2B)(b)(ii), (bb), (d))?
GIVEN `I was wholly dependent on the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were wholly (not just partly) dependent on the worker for support
      `I have married since the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have married since the worker's death
      `I now live with someone as a couple without being married to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you now live with another person on a permanent and genuine domestic basis, although not legally married to them
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the weekly spouse payment payable to me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I have married since the death` THEN JUST FALSE  -- "until the marriage"
           IF `I now live with someone as a couple without being married to them` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 8(2B)(bb)
           IF (NOT `I was wholly dependent on the worker`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 8(2B)(d): what the Authority determines)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 8(2B)(b)(iii) "in the case of a surviving spouse and subject to paragraph (ba)--a weekly payment of $69.40 per week in
-- respect of each child who was wholly or partly dependent on the worker for support, to continue until the death of that
-- child." (ba) "The payment ... shall not be made in respect of a child who has attained, or attains, the age of 16 years
-- unless the child is under the age of 21 years and is receiving full-time education at a school, college or
-- university." (e) a child includes a stepchild and a child to whom the worker stood in loco parentis. With no surviving
-- spouse, s 8(2B) does not apply to children alone (s 8(2AA)): JUST FALSE. The figure is adjustable (finding 2).
@export If section 8(2B) applies, is the weekly payment for this child of the worker payable on this day (s 8(2B)(b)(iii), (ba), (e))?
GIVEN `the worker left a surviving spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker left a surviving spouse
      `the child depended on the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child (including a stepchild, or a child to whom the worker stood in the place of a parent) was wholly or partly dependent on the worker for support
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The child's date of birth
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (for example today)
      `the child is in full-time education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on that day, the child is receiving full-time education at a school, college or university
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the weekly payment for this child payable` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the worker left a surviving spouse`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- "in the case of a surviving spouse"; s 8(2AA)
           IF (NOT `the child depended on the worker`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- "each child who was wholly or partly dependent"
           IF `the age` LESS THAN 16 THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the age` LESS THAN 21 AND `the child is in full-time education` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- (ba) "shall not ... unless"
    WHERE
        `the age` MEANS `the age on` `the day asked about` `of someone born on` `the child's date of birth`

-- s 8(2D)(b) "All weekly compensation prescribed by subsection (2B) or (2C) as payable in respect of a child of a worker
-- shall--(i) where the worker left a surviving spouse, be paid to such surviving spouse unless the Authority otherwise
-- orders, (ii) where the worker did not leave a surviving spouse or where the Authority otherwise orders under
-- subparagraph (i), be paid to such person or institution as the Authority may direct."
@export Who is paid the weekly payment for the worker's child (s 8(2D)(b))?
GIVEN `the worker left a surviving spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker left a surviving spouse
      `the Authority has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has ordered that the child's payment be paid to someone other than the surviving spouse
GIVETH A `Who is paid for the child`
`Who is paid for the child's weekly payment` MEANS
    IF `the worker left a surviving spouse` AND (NOT `the Authority has ordered otherwise`)
    THEN `the surviving spouse`
    ELSE `the person or institution the Authority directs`

-- s 8(2E)(a): at the dependent person's request, the Authority "may, if it considers it to be in the best interests of
-- that person", redeem weekly payments by a lump sum. (b): it "shall not" award a lump sum that, added to the weekly
-- payments since the death and any other lump sum, "would exceed the amount of the lump sum that would have been payable
-- to a surviving spouse of the worker under Division 1 of Part 3 of the Principal Act at the time of the death". The
-- answer is the most (never below 0); whether to redeem at all is the Authority's judgment.
@export If I ask the Authority to redeem my weekly payments with a lump sum, what is the most that lump sum can be (s 8(2E))?
GIVEN `the spouse lump sum under the 1987 Act at the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The lump sum, in dollars, that would have been payable to a surviving spouse of the worker under Division 1 of Part 3 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 at the time of the death
      `the weekly payments I have received since the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the weekly payments, in dollars, payable to you under this Act from the worker's death to the date of the redemption
      `the other lump sums I have received` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of any other lump sum, in dollars, payable to you under this Act
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most a redemption lump sum can be` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 `and` (`the spouse lump sum under the 1987 Act at the death` MINUS (`the weekly payments I have received since the death` PLUS `the other lump sums I have received`))

§§ `s 8(3A), (3B), (6A) -- the date of injury and the rate`

-- s 8(3A): for the Principal Act and the 1998 Act, "the injury ... shall be deemed to have happened at the time when that
-- person was last employed as a worker in an occupation to the nature of which the disease contracted by him was due";
-- proviso: if the Authority, on the panel's report, is satisfied that employment did not materially contribute, it "may"
-- disregard it and look to the last previous employment that did. Conditional on the Authority having done so.
@export When is my injury taken to have happened for the workers compensation Acts (s 8(3A))?
GIVEN `the last day I was employed as a worker in the occupation` IS A DATE @desc The last day you were employed as a worker in an occupation to the nature of which your dust disease was due
      `the Authority has disregarded that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority, on the panel's report, being satisfied that this last employment did not materially contribute to your disablement or death, has decided to disregard it
      `the last day of the previous employment that contributed` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your last previous employment that the Authority is satisfied did materially contribute (any day if the Authority has not disregarded the last employment)
GIVETH A DATE
`When is my injury taken to have happened` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has disregarded that employment`
    THEN `the last day of the previous employment that contributed`
    ELSE `the last day I was employed as a worker in the occupation`

-- s 8(3B) "Where the Authority is satisfied that a person who ... is receiving or entitled to receive weekly payments ...
-- in respect of the person's partial disablement ... has taken all reasonable steps to obtain, and has failed to obtain
-- employment of a kind suited to a person so partially disabled, and that the person's failure ... is a consequence,
-- wholly or mainly, of such disablement the Authority may order that the person's disablement shall be treated as total
-- disablement". "Where" fails: JUST FALSE. Conditions met, no order: the Authority "may" -- NOTHING. An order in force:
-- JUST TRUE ("While such an order remains in force").
@export I am paid for a partial disablement: will my disablement be treated as total because I cannot find suitable work (s 8(3B))?
GIVEN `I receive weekly payments for a partial disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving, or entitled to receive, weekly payments under an award for partial disablement for work from a dust disease
      `I have taken all reasonable steps to find suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is satisfied that you have taken all reasonable steps to obtain work of a kind suited to a person with your partial disablement
      `I have failed to find suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to obtain such work
      `the failure is wholly or mainly because of my disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is satisfied that the failure is a consequence, wholly or mainly, of your disablement
      `the Authority has ordered it and not rescinded the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has ordered your disablement to be treated as total, and that order has not been rescinded
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Will my partial disablement be treated as total` MEANS
    IF (NOT (    `I receive weekly payments for a partial disablement`
             AND `I have taken all reasonable steps to find suitable work`
             AND `I have failed to find suitable work`
             AND `the failure is wholly or mainly because of my disablement`))
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- "where" fails
    ELSE IF `the Authority has ordered it and not rescinded the order`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the Authority "may" order; not yet done)

-- s 8(6A): where the Authority found the person a worker during only part of the time and is of the opinion, on the
-- panel's report, that the disablement or death was "to a substantial extent attributable" to exposure while not a
-- worker, it "shall ... fix the rate ... at such rate, being a lesser rate than would otherwise have been payable". The
-- duty to reduce is the Act's ("shall"); how much is the Authority's.
@export Must the Authority pay me (or my family) at a lesser rate because much of the exposure to dust was while not a worker (s 8(6A))?
GIVEN `the Authority found a worker for only part of the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority found that the person was a worker during only part of the time engaged in the occupation
      `the Authority is of opinion much exposure was outside worker time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is of the opinion, on the panel's report, that the disablement or death was to a substantial extent attributable to exposure to dust while the person was engaged in the occupation otherwise than as a worker (for example self-employed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the rate be reduced for exposure outside worker time` MEANS
    IF `the Authority found a worker for only part of the time` AND `the Authority is of opinion much exposure was outside worker time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- "where": the text's no

§§ `s 8(6), s 11 -- compensation under other Acts`

-- s 8(6)(a): a person claiming or receiving compensation under this Act "shall not be entitled to claim or receive, in
-- respect of that part of the person's disablement ... in respect of which the person is claiming or receiving
-- compensation under this Act, ... compensation under the Principal Act or under any other Act ... relating to
-- compensation to ... workers". A flat negative; another part, or no claim under this Act, is not addressed: NOTHING.
@export Can I also claim workers compensation under the 1987 Act or another NSW compensation Act for the same disablement (s 8(6)(a))?
GIVEN `I claim or receive dust diseases compensation for that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are claiming or receiving compensation under the Dust Diseases Act for the same part of your disablement (or the same death)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I also claim under the 1987 Act for the same disablement` MEANS
    IF `I claim or receive dust diseases compensation for that part`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- "shall not be entitled"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent on another part, or where no claim is made under this Act)

-- s 8(6)(b): where compensation for a death would be payable under this Act and the Principal Act (or another compensation
-- Act), and the other Act's compensation "(i) would be of the same or of a lesser amount ..., no compensation shall be
-- payable under the Principal Act ..., or (ii) would exceed the compensation payable under this Act ..., the compensation
-- payable under the Principal Act ... shall be reduced by the amount of compensation payable under this Act". The
-- weekly payments under this Act count as a capital sum the Authority assesses: asked.
@export For the same death, how much can still be paid under the 1987 Act or another compensation Act on top of the dust diseases compensation (s 8(6)(b))?
GIVEN `the compensation under the other Act for the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensation, in dollars, that would otherwise be payable for the death under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 or another NSW workers compensation Act
      `the compensation under this Act for the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensation, in dollars, payable for the death under the Dust Diseases Act (weekly payments other than for a child counted as the capital sum the Authority assesses)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can still be paid under the other Act for the death` MEANS
    IF `the compensation under the other Act for the death` AT MOST `the compensation under this Act for the death`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the compensation under the other Act for the death` MINUS `the compensation under this Act for the death`

-- s 8(6)(c): where (i) the weekly amount under this Act plus (ii) the weekly amount under the Principal Act or another
-- compensation Act would exceed the greater of (iii) the weekly payments for total disablement under this Act and (iv)
-- the weekly payments for total incapacity under the other Act, "the weekly payments ... under the Principal Act or under
-- the said compensation Act shall be reduced by an amount equal to the difference". The reduction is never below 0, and
-- cannot be more than the other Act's weekly amount (fork F4).
@export By how much is my weekly workers compensation under the 1987 Act (or another Act) reduced because I also get dust diseases weekly payments (s 8(6)(c))?
GIVEN `my weekly dust diseases payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount per week, in dollars, payable to you under the Dust Diseases Act for your disablement
      `my weekly payment under the other Act` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount per week, in dollars, that would otherwise be payable to you under the Workers Compensation Act 1987 or another compensation Act
      `the weekly payment for total disablement under this Act` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly payment, in dollars, you would receive under the Dust Diseases Act for total disablement from the disease
      `the weekly payment for total incapacity under the other Act` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly payment, in dollars, you would receive under the other Act for total incapacity for work
GIVETH A NUMBER
`By how much is my other weekly compensation reduced` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`the larger of` 0 `and` (`the total` MINUS `the ceiling`)) `and` `my weekly payment under the other Act`
    WHERE
        `the total` MEANS `my weekly dust diseases payment` PLUS `my weekly payment under the other Act`
        `the ceiling` MEANS `the larger of` `the weekly payment for total disablement under this Act` `and` `the weekly payment for total incapacity under the other Act`

-- s 11(1): if Schedule 1 is amended to include a disease, "(a) the amendment operates to extinguish an entitlement to
-- compensation under the Principal Act in respect of that disease existing immediately before the amendment unless an
-- application for compensation in respect of the entitlement is made before the amendment". (2) "Subsection (1) (a)
-- does not operate to extinguish a person's entitlement to compensation if the person does not have an entitlement to
-- compensation under this Act in respect of the matter concerned." "Unless" and a flat "does not": JUST FALSE.
@export My disease was added to the list of dust diseases after I became entitled under the 1987 Act: is my 1987 Act entitlement extinguished (s 11)?
GIVEN `I had a 1987 Act entitlement for the disease before it was added` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before the disease was added to Schedule 1, you had an entitlement to compensation for it under the Workers Compensation Act 1987
      `I applied under the 1987 Act before it was added` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made an application for compensation for that entitlement before the disease was added to Schedule 1
      `I have an entitlement under this Act for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an entitlement to compensation under the Dust Diseases Act for the same matter
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my 1987 Act entitlement extinguished` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I had a 1987 Act entitlement for the disease before it was added`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (nothing to extinguish; s 11 is silent)
           IF `I applied under the 1987 Act before it was added` THEN JUST FALSE  -- "unless an application ... is made before"
           IF (NOT `I have an entitlement under this Act for it`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 11(2) "does not operate"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 8(7), (8) -- from when weekly payments run`

-- s 8(7) "Weekly compensation payments under an award made pursuant to subsection (1) (a) shall be payable as from the
-- date when the application for compensation is received by the Authority or, if the Authority, subject to subsection
-- (8), determines that those payments should be payable as from an earlier date, as from that earlier date." (8) "The
-- Authority shall not ... determine a date earlier than 29th February 1968, or earlier than the date of disablement".
GIVEN `the day I was disabled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day weekly payments can be backdated to` `the day I was disabled` MEANS
    `the later of` (`the date` 29 2 1968) `and` `the day I was disabled`

@export What is the earliest day the Authority can backdate my weekly payments to (s 8(7), (8))?
GIVEN `the day the Authority received my application` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority received your application for compensation
      `the day I was disabled` IS A DATE @desc The date of your disablement (the date from which you were disabled for work by the dust disease)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest day my weekly payments can be backdated to` MEANS
    IF `the day the Authority received my application` `is before` `the floor`
    THEN `the day the Authority received my application`
    ELSE `the floor`
    WHERE
        `the floor` MEANS `the earliest day weekly payments can be backdated to` `the day I was disabled`

-- A determined date before the floor is one the Authority "shall not" determine; the Act does not say what then
-- follows: NOTHING (fork F5). A determined date after the application date is not "earlier": the application date.
@export From what day are my weekly payments payable (s 8(7), (8))?
GIVEN `the day the Authority received my application` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority received your application for compensation
      `the day I was disabled` IS A DATE @desc The date of your disablement
      `the Authority determined an earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority determined that your weekly payments should run from a day earlier than the day it received your application
      `the earlier day the Authority determined` IS A DATE @desc The earlier day the Authority determined (any day if it did not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`From what day are my weekly payments payable` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the Authority determined an earlier day`) THEN JUST `the day the Authority received my application`
           IF (NOT (`the earlier day the Authority determined` `is before` `the day the Authority received my application`)) THEN JUST `the day the Authority received my application`
           IF `the earlier day the Authority determined` `is before` (`the earliest day weekly payments can be backdated to` `the day I was disabled`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 8(8) forbids it; the effect is not stated; fork F5)
           OTHERWISE JUST `the earlier day the Authority determined`

§§ `s 8AA -- compensation received elsewhere`

-- s 8AA(1) "prescribed engagement means engagement ... in an occupation--(a) as an employee within the meaning of the
-- Commonwealth Employees Compensation Act 1930 ..., or (b) under a contract of service or apprenticeship outside New
-- South Wales." (2)(a) the subsection applies to a person who has received or is receiving compensation under a law of
-- the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country, for disablement from (or another's death from) a
-- dust disease contracted in a prescribed engagement. (b) such a person, if they (or the person who died) were not
-- "after the cessation of the person's prescribed engagement engaged as a worker in an occupation to the nature of which
-- the disease was due", is not entitled to compensation from the Fund for that part. The answer is "am I barred?"; a
-- bar that does not arise is JUST FALSE (the text's "applies to" is a closed description).
@export Am I barred from dust diseases compensation because I have received compensation elsewhere (s 8AA(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I have received compensation under another law for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received or are receiving compensation for this disablement (or death) from a dust disease under a law of the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country
      `how I was engaged` IS A `How I was engaged when I contracted the disease` @desc How the disease was contracted. One of: "as a Commonwealth employee under Commonwealth employees compensation law", "under a contract of service or apprenticeship outside New South Wales", "in some other way"
      `I later worked as a worker in an occupation that causes the disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after that engagement ended, you (or the person who died) worked as a worker in an occupation to the nature of which the disease was due
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I barred because I was compensated elsewhere` MEANS
    IF     `I have received compensation under another law for it`
       AND `the engagement is prescribed`
       AND (NOT `I later worked as a worker in an occupation that causes the disease`)
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- barred for that part (s 8AA(2)(b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the engagement is prescribed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how I was engaged`
            WHEN `in some other way` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 8AA(3): every person receiving or claiming compensation from the Fund "shall, on receiving any compensation under an
-- Act (other than this Act), ordinance or other law referred to in subsection (2) ... or on being notified of his or her
-- entitlement to any compensation ..., inform the Authority of such receipt or notification within 7 days thereafter and
-- if the person does not do so shall be guilty of an offence against this Act and be liable to a penalty not exceeding 1
-- penalty unit." Time 0 is the day of receipt or notification, in days. s 8AA(5): "No person shall be liable by virtue of
-- any provisions of this section to repay any money paid from the Fund."
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 8AA(3) -- the claimant must inform the Authority within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `inform the Authority of the other compensation`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "the Authority was not informed within 7 days of receiving, or being notified of an entitlement to, compensation under another law (s 8AA(3)); an offence with a maximum penalty of 1 penalty unit"

@export If I receive, or am told I am entitled to, compensation under another law for my dust disease, by what day must I tell the Authority (s 8AA(3))?
GIVEN `the day I received it or was notified` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the other compensation, or were notified of your entitlement to it, whichever came first
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I tell the Authority about other compensation` MEANS
    `the day I received it or was notified` `plus days` 7

@export Have I told the Dust Diseases Authority about my other compensation in time (s 8AA(3))?
GIVEN `I claim or receive compensation from the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are claiming or receiving compensation from the Dust Diseases Fund
      `I received or was notified of compensation under another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received, or been notified of an entitlement to, compensation for the disablement or death under a law of the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country
      `the day I received it or was notified` IS A DATE @desc The day you received it or were notified (any day if not)
      `I have informed the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have informed the Authority of it
      `the day I informed the Authority` IS A DATE @desc The day you informed the Authority (any day if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What section 8AA(3) means for me`
`Have I told the Authority in time` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`I claim or receive compensation from the Fund` AND `I received or was notified of compensation under another law`)) THEN `section 8AA(3) puts no duty on me`
           IF `I have informed the Authority` THEN
               CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 8AA(3) -- the claimant must inform the Authority within 7 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `inform the Authority of the other compensation` `the time informed`))
               WHEN FULFILLED THEN `I informed the Authority within the 7 days`
               OTHERWISE `I have not informed the Authority within the 7 days, an offence with a maximum penalty of 1 penalty unit`
           IF `the days from` `the day I received it or was notified` `to` `today` AT MOST 7 THEN `I have not yet informed the Authority, and the 7 days have not ended`
           OTHERWISE `I have not informed the Authority within the 7 days, an offence with a maximum penalty of 1 penalty unit`
    WHERE
        `the raw time` MEANS `the days from` `the day I received it or was notified` `to` `the day I informed the Authority`
        `the time informed` MEANS IF `the raw time` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `the raw time`

§§ `s 8B -- interim award`

-- s 8B(1): an interim award "as does not exceed the least compensation to which the person is, in the opinion of the
-- Authority, entitled". (2) on the final award "the amounts which have been paid under the interim award shall be
-- deducted from the amount payable under the award". Interim payments larger than the final award: the Act is silent
-- (and s 8B says nothing of repayment): NOTHING.
@export After my final award, how much is still payable once the interim award payments are deducted (s 8B(2))?
GIVEN `the amount payable under the final award` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, payable under the final award made under s 8(1)
      `the amount paid under the interim award` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, already paid to you under the interim award
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is still payable after the interim award` MEANS
    IF `the amount paid under the interim award` GREATER THAN `the amount payable under the final award`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent on an overpayment)
    ELSE JUST (`the amount payable under the final award` MINUS `the amount paid under the interim award`)

§§ `s 8I -- appeal`

-- s 8I(1) "If a person affected by a decision of the Authority or the Medical Assessment Panel in relation to a claim for
-- compensation under this Act is dissatisfied with the decision, the person may appeal against the decision to the
-- District Court". (1A) "An appeal under subsection (1) must be made within 6 months after notice of the decision appealed
-- against has been given to the appellant." Time 0 is the day notice is given, in days; the rule is a condition on the
-- power to appeal, written with DO (neither required nor forbidden): after the deadline the right has lapsed.
GIVEN `the days in the six months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 8I(1A) -- an appeal must be made within 6 months after notice of the decision` `the days in the six months` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    DO `appeal to the District Court`
    WITHIN `the days in the six months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "no appeal made within 6 months after notice of the decision was given (s 8I(1A)); the time to appeal has passed"

@export By what day must I appeal to the District Court against a decision of the Authority or the Medical Assessment Panel (s 8I(1A))?
GIVEN `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the decision was given to you
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I appeal` MEANS `the day I was given notice of the decision` `plus months` 6

@export Can I appeal to the District Court on the day I plan to (s 8I(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `I am affected by the decision and dissatisfied with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person affected by a decision of the Authority or the Medical Assessment Panel on a claim under the Act, and dissatisfied with it
      `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the decision was given to you
      `the day I plan to appeal` IS A DATE @desc The day you would file the appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I appeal on that day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am affected by the decision and dissatisfied with it`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 8I gives the right to an affected person; it is silent on others)
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 8I(1A) -- an appeal must be made within 6 months after notice of the decision` `the six months`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `appeal to the District Court` `the appeal time`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- a period fixed in the text's own words
    WHERE
        `the six months` MEANS `the days from` `the day I was given notice of the decision` `to` (`By when must I appeal` `the day I was given notice of the decision`)
        `the raw appeal time` MEANS `the days from` `the day I was given notice of the decision` `to` `the day I plan to appeal`
        `the appeal time` MEANS IF `the raw appeal time` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `the raw appeal time`

§§ `s 9A -- the costs of being examined`

-- s 9A(1) "A worker who is required under this Act to submit for a medical examination is entitled to be reimbursed by
-- the Authority for--(a) the amount of any wages lost by the worker by reason of submitting for examination, and (b) the
-- costs of any fares, travelling expenses and maintenance necessarily and reasonably incurred in submitting for
-- examination." A grant limited by its own words: outside it, NOTHING.
@export Can I be reimbursed for this cost of going to a medical examination the Act requires (s 9A)?
GIVEN `I am required under the Act to submit for the examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker required under the Dust Diseases Act (for example by the Authority or the regulations) to submit for a medical examination
      `the cost` IS A `The examination cost` @desc The cost you are asking about. One of: "wages I lost by submitting for the examination", "fares, travelling expenses or maintenance", "some other cost"
      `it was necessarily and reasonably incurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For fares, travelling expenses or maintenance: whether the cost was necessarily and reasonably incurred in submitting for the examination
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be reimbursed for this examination cost` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am required under the Act to submit for the examination`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 9A is silent on an examination the Act does not require)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the cost`
         WHEN `wages I lost by submitting for the examination` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `fares, travelling expenses or maintenance` THEN
             IF `it was necessarily and reasonably incurred`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited by its own wording)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent on other costs)

§§ `Sch 2 cll 20, 21 -- retired and unemployed workers`

-- Sch 2 cl 20(1) "For the purposes of this Act, the Principal Act, section 37(1)(b) and (c), as in force by operation of
-- the exclusion provisions, is taken to extend to an injured worker in relation to any period of partial incapacity for
-- work but only if the injured worker is retired by reason of--(a) reaching an applicable retirement age, or (b) being
-- unfit for suitable employment as a result of a dust disease." "But only if": JUST FALSE otherwise. A worker who is not
-- retired is not what cl 20 addresses: NOTHING (s 37 applies as it stands).
-- This situation only arises for a retired worker.
@export I am retired and partially incapacitated by a dust disease: do the 1987 Act's weekly payments for partial incapacity after the first 26 weeks (s 37(1)(b), (c)) extend to me (Sch 2 cl 20)?
GIVEN `I am retired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are retired
      `why I am retired` IS A `Why I am retired` @desc Why you are retired. One of: "I reached an applicable retirement age", "I am unfit for suitable employment as a result of a dust disease", "some other reason"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do the partial incapacity weekly payments extend to me though retired` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am retired`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (cl 20 addresses only a retired worker)
    ELSE CONSIDER `why I am retired`
         WHEN `some other reason` THEN JUST FALSE  -- "but only if"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Sch 2 cl 21(1) "This clause applies to an injured worker in relation to any period of total incapacity for work if the
-- worker is retired or unemployed." (2) current weekly wage rate means "(a) the amount estimated by the Australian Bureau
-- of Statistics as the average weekly total cash earnings of all employees in New South Wales for the week immediately
-- before the worker was incapacitated" (or, if the ABS stops estimating it, the prescribed amount). (3) "Subclause (2)
-- does not apply if the worker produces evidence about actual wages earned before the first 26 weeks of incapacity and
-- requests the rate be determined in accordance with the Principal Act, section 42".
-- This situation only arises for a retired or unemployed worker.
@export I am retired or unemployed and totally incapacitated: what wage figure sets my weekly payments (Sch 2 cl 21)?
GIVEN `I am totally incapacitated for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are totally incapacitated for work by the dust disease
      `I am retired or unemployed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are retired or unemployed
      `I gave evidence of my actual wages and asked for section 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you produced evidence of the actual wages you earned before the first 26 weeks of incapacity and asked for the rate to be worked out under section 42 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987
GIVETH A `The wage figure`
`Which wage figure sets my weekly payments` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`I am totally incapacitated for work` AND `I am retired or unemployed`)) THEN `clause 21 does not apply to me`
           IF `I gave evidence of my actual wages and asked for section 42` THEN `my actual wages, worked out under section 42 of the 1987 Act at my request`
           OTHERWISE `the ABS average weekly total cash earnings of all NSW employees for the week before I was incapacitated`
